        "input": {
          "level": "preferred",
          "summary": "Replace mandatory ICC arbitration (seat Osaka/New York) with exclusive jurisdiction of the New York County courts, preserving temporary injunctive relief elsewhere.",
          "comment": "[Playbook] New York law already governs, but disputes go to three-arbitrator ICC arbitration that can be seated in Osaka, which sits outside our accepted position of courts rather than foreign arbitration. We have replaced the arbitration referral and its procedural machinery with exclusive jurisdiction of the state and federal courts in New York County, keeping each Party's ability to seek temporary injunctive relief in any other court.",
          "precedentId": "seed-govlaw",
